            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdomen due to adenomyosis of the uterus: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Japanese woman with severe abdominal pain underwent an emergent exploratory laparotomy. Intraperitoneal bleeding from the uterine serosal surface was observed, and a pathologic examination showed that the bleeding was caused by an exudative hemorrhage from the endometrial tissues in the myometrium close to the uterine serosal surface.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
